<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (1\) Corporate Management:)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 462 0 R
/ActualText (Each corporation has a unique identity within the database and operates multiple routes. Corporations may share stops and routes for intercity or interstate connectivity.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2\) Stop Characteristics:)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 463 0 R
/ActualText (Stops are uniquely identified by their IDs, and multiple routes can utilize the same stop. Stops are classified into two categories: normal stops and stations, differentiated by their type value.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3\) Trip Operations:)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 464 0 R
/ActualText (A trip represents a single vehicle journey along a route and includes intermediate stops. Each trip is governed by a service schedule defined by a calendar and service dates.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4\) Schedules:)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
